---
import ServiceLayout from '../../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import GoldenList from '../../components/GoldenList.astro';
import GlassCard from '../../components/GlassCard.astro';
---

<ServiceLayout
  title="Velocity Funnel Architecture"
  subtitle="High-Octane Conversion Systems. From Click to Close in Under 10 Minutes."
  metaDescription="Most websites are digital brochures. We build conversion engines. Sub-second load times. Psychological triggers. Automated qualification."
>

  <h2>The "Brochure Website" Problem</h2>
  <p>
    If you are sending paid traffic to your homepage (the one with the "About Us" and "Blog" links), you are setting money on fire. The average corporate website converts cold traffic at 0.5% - 1%. That means for every $100 you spend on ads, you might get one lead worth $50. The math doesn't work.
  </p>
  <p>
    A <strong>Funnel</strong> is not a website. It is a linear, psychological journey designed to do one thing: <strong>Extract a qualified booked appointment from a total stranger.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    We replace your passive website with an active <strong>Filtration Architecture</strong>.
  </p>

  <hr class="border-white/10 my-12" />

  <h2>The Architecture: The "Pre-Suasion" Protocol</h2>
  <p>
    We don't just "design pages." We engineer decision paths. Our funnels utilize the Cialdini "Pre-Suasion" framework to handle objections <em>before</em> they are even raised.
  </p>

  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 my-12 not-prose">
    <div class="p-6 bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-sm">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4 font-mono">Standard Landing Page</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-400 text-sm">
        <li class="flex gap-2">❌ "Learn More" CTAs</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">❌ Slow Loading (3s+)</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">❌ Generic Stock Photos</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2">❌ 12 Navigation Links (Distraction)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="p-6 bg-gold-900/10 border border-gold-500/30 rounded-sm relative overflow-hidden">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4 font-mono">Velocity Architecture</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-100 text-sm font-medium">
        <li class="flex gap-2 text-gold-400">⚡ "Direct Offer" Logic</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2 text-gold-400">⚡ Sub-Second Load (Astro/Edge)</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2 text-gold-400">⚡ VSL (Video Sales Letter) Core</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2 text-gold-400">⚡ Zero Exit Points (Linear)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Technology Stack: Speed is Revenue</h2>
  <p>
    Amazon found that every 100ms of latency cost them 1% in sales. In the B2B world, attention spans are even shorter. We do not use WordPress, Wix, or ClickFunnels. These platforms are bloated legacy tech.
  </p>
  <p>
    We build on <strong>Astro + Tailwind + Edge Computing</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    This creates pages that load instantly (0.2s). The user clicks the ad, and the page is *there*. No white screen. No spinner. Just your offer, instantly. This simple technical shift often boosts conversion rates by 30% overnight.
  </p>

  <h2>The 4-Step "Filtration" Flow</h2>
  <p>
    We do not want "leads." We want "qualified opportunities." A lead is a name and email. An opportunity is someone with money, pain, and intent. Our funnel filters the noise out.
  </p>

  <div class="my-12">
    <GoldenList 
      iconType="circuit"
      items={[
        "<strong>Step 1: The Hook (Landing Page):</strong> Focuses entirely on the 'Bleeding Neck' problem. No fluff. Just the solution.",
        "<strong>Step 2: The Education (VSL):</strong> A 5-15 minute video that shifts their belief system. It explains *why* your method is the only logical choice.",
        "<strong>Step 3: The Application (Filter):</strong> A rigorous questionnaire. We ask revenue, timeline, and budget. If they don't qualify, they don't get your calendar.",
        "<strong>Step 4: The Commitment (Booking):</strong> They select a time and put down a deposit (optional) or commit to attending."
      ]}
    />
  </div>

  <h2>Psychological Mechanics: The "Micro-Commitment"</h2>
  <p>
    We never ask for marriage on the first date. We use <strong>Micro-Commitments</strong>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't flip the "Book a Call" button immediately.</li>
    <li>We first ask: "Is your business doing over $20k/mo?" (Easy YES).</li>
    <li>Then: "Are you the owner?" (Easy YES).</li>
    <li>By the time we ask for the phone number, they have already said "YES" to you 5 times. The brain seeks consistency. They are chemically wired to finish the form.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr class="border-white/10 my-12" />

  <h2>Technical Specifications</h2>
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 not-prose">
    <GlassCard title="A/B Testing Rig">
      <p class="text-sm mt-4 text-gray-400">
        Every funnel we deploy comes with <strong>VWO or Google Optimize</strong> installed. We are constantly testing Headlines, VSL Hooks, and Button Colors. A 5% lift in conversion here doubles your profit margin.
      </p>
    </GlassCard>
    <GlassCard title="CRM Integration">
      <p class="text-sm mt-4 text-gray-400">
        Data flows instantly into your CRM (HubSpot, GoHighLevel, Salesforce). We tag the lead with "High Priority" if they match your ICP, triggering instant SMS alerts to your sales team.
      </p>
    </GlassCard>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-16 p-8 border border-gold-500/30 bg-gold-900/5 rounded-lg text-center">
    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Is Your Funnel Leaking Revenue?</h3>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-8">
      Let us run a stress test on your current architecture.
    </p>
    <a href="/#audit" class="inline-block px-8 py-4 bg-gold-500 hover:bg-gold-400 text-black font-bold uppercase tracking-widest rounded-sm transition-colors">
      Start Funnel Audit
    </a>
  </div>

</ServiceLayout>
